WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.920
(upbeat music)

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:05.100
- [Reporter] The McAloo Tikki
burger, McPops, onion rings.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.050
If you don't recognize these items

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.120
from your regular McDonald's menu,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.800
that's because you can't get them

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.770
at a regular McDonald's in the US.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.330
They're exclusive to McDonald's

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.959
in their respective countries.

00:00:16.959 --> 00:00:18.872
♪ The all-new McAloo Tikki ♪

00:00:18.872 --> 00:00:19.705
♪ $2 ♪

00:00:19.705 --> 00:00:21.510
- [Reporter] Designed to
both attract tourists.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.420
- [Tourist] America does not
have these fries or wings.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.040
- [Reporter] And more importantly,

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.840
drive international sales.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.580
- When you look at the sales figures,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.700
about 41% of their sales are in the US

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.320
and all the rest are international.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.090
- [Newsreader] Here's how and why

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.360
the company designs those local menus.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.537
This is "The Economics of
McDonald's International."

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.690
McDonald's founder, Ray Kroc

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.200
opened his first restaurant
in Illinois in 1955

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.840
with just three food items on the menu.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.140
Its staple was a 15 cent hamburger.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:59.220
It first moved outside the
continental US in 1967.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.370
Now the company has
over 40,000 restaurants

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.800
in over 100 countries.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.260
- We think of McDonald's
as an American company,

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.380
and in the US they have
about 13,500 restaurants.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.730
But the bulk of their restaurants

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.020
are actually international.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.460
So all the rest of those restaurants,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.310
about 27,000, are all around the world.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.300
- [Reporter] And you may have noticed

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.130
that the restaurants look different.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.870
- This is so chic.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.990
There's no Grimace, no Hamburglar.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.878
- [Heather] In Canada they offer poutine.

00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:30.360
(narrator speaking French)

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.740
- [Reporter] While global core items

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.420
like burgers and fries

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.880
make up most of McDonald's
food sales still,

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.450
these local menu items make up about 30%.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.750
International sales are a key
part of McDonald's revenue.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.530
Australia, China, Japan,
France, and Germany

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:49.290
are a few of the company's top markets.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:50.700
Adopting a menu like this

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.030
is a strategy companies
use called localization,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.310
and it's a tactic that has been essential

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.320
to McDonald's global growth.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.350
When the company expanded
into India in 1996,

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.840
it did so without any beef on its menus.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.910
observing the common belief in the country

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.710
that cows are sacred.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.530
McDonald's served more than
6 million customers there

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.260
its first year with items
like the Maharaja Mac,

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.850
made with mutton patties.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:17.610
One of India's current
popular items is this,

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.320
the McAloo Tikki Burger.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.390
- It's a potato and pea patty

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.850
blended with some Indian spices.

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.470
- [Reporter] This is Roger Di Domenico.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.040
He works with local teams to
build international menus.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.640
- They remind me of a
certain Indian Street food

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.020
that I had growing up.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.380
So I think it's just a
wonderful way to recognize

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.850
and get closer to the customers

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.680
while still remaining McDonald's.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.810
- [Reporter] Most McDonald's
locations globally

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:46.530
are managed and owned by
franchisees or licensees

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.030
rather than the company.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.800
Deciding what's on those menus

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.930
starts with customer research.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:55.890
Local experts use that
research to craft new items.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.070
Local flavors are
incorporated in several ways.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.290
The first is adapting McDonald's staples

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:03.540
to fit specific tastes.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.910
- I think if you look at
the Spicy Chicken McNuggets

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.230
that have been in multiple markets,

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:10.320
each one of those markets has
a different interpretation

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.360
of what spice means to their consumers.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.090
There'll be one that might
be highlighting curry.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.160
There might be one that highlights

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.080
more of a Tabasco-like flavor.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.430
And then a third one
that will use something

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.410
like a Thai chili or a jalapeno.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:23.250
- [Reporter] But some markets

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.214
will create or offer
something completely new.

00:03:26.214 --> 00:03:29.940
Mexico has McMolletes
as part of breakfast.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.240
The Philippines serves fried
chicken with McSpaghetti.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.670
- If it's something that tastes like home

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.420
and can be both true to McDonald's
and true to the consumer,

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.920
it's a big win for us.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.380
- [Reporter] And some additions
to the international menus

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.480
compete with other restaurants.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.900
- In some of these countries,
McDonald's definitely competes

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.180
with a brand like KFC on chicken.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.415
So in some countries in the Middle East,

00:03:53.415 --> 00:03:55.270
they actually offer fried chicken,

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:58.140
which is not something
you'd see on US menus.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.780
But to compete with these
local flavors, they do that.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.330
- [Reporter] Some of the more
popular international items

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:06.420
have even spread to
McDonald's menus globally.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.190
- McFlurry started off in Canada

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.020
and now it's loved everywhere.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.150
McSpicy is a product that started off

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.550
as a local taste variation in China

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:17.130
that has now been adopted
all over the world.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:20.340
We want people to come in
for the global core icons.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.620
We want people to come
in to try something new.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:25.620
And so any of the menu items
that we feel like will do that

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.380
is what we wanna elevate in the system.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.390
- [Reporter] McDonald's
seized on the popularity

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.700
of South Korean boy band BTS,

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:35.190
launching a limited edition BTS meal

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:37.590
in a number of countries in 2021.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.930
It included sweet chili and Cajun sauces

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.330
inspired by the South Korean market.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.490
The company said the
promotion helped drive

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:48.180
a 40% increase from the
year before in global sales

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.911
and significantly lifted McNugget
sales during that period.

00:04:51.911 --> 00:04:52.744
(BTS singing)

00:04:52.744 --> 00:04:55.350
But some transplants aren't so successful.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.730
- For a number of years

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.880
McDonald's has had a
McVegan sandwich in Germany

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.470
and some other European countries.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:04.980
They recently tried offering
what they called a McPlant,

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:08.190
which was using a Beyond
Meat burger in the US,

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.260
and they tested that in some markets.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.500
And it just doesn't seem the
consumers here want that.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.720
So, you know, there is a push, pull.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.900
You know, it's fun to have
new flavors, it's exciting,

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.951
but it doesn't always
work in a permanent way.

00:05:20.951 --> 00:05:21.784
(slow music)

00:05:21.784 --> 00:05:22.680
- [Reporter] While having a wide selection

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.750
of items globally is profitable,

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.170
McDonald's is looking to
streamline some of its offerings.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:31.200
- This year the CEO, Chris K has said

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.180
that there's just too many redundancies

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.590
all across the world.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.210
He gave an example where, you know,

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.520
there's 70 different types
of chicken sandwiches

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.900
all across the world.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.690
And so I think they are in
the process of examining that,

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:43.722
but I don't think they're gonna eliminate

00:05:43.722 --> 00:05:45.990
all local items on menus.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.760
- [Reporter] So next time you're in Spain

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.100
you might be able to try McPops.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.540
- They're filled with your choice

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.220
of white chocolate or hazelnut.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.210
They're super soft

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.760
and they've got this amazing
filling on the inside.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.240
Can I bother for a napkin?

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.763
- [Speaker] Yeah, napkin (indistinct).

00:06:02.886 --> 00:06:05.636
(Roger laughing)

